    pr_ref:  # 1d01
    description: "Found by the mulul run (branch jgstern-agent/fix/mulul-catalogue-rows) while pinning INV-zufiz's haskell flow.\n\nREPRO on dev e58250d (main checkout code, unmodified): Main.hs = `import System.Process (readProcess)`; `main = do { out <- readProcess \"ls\" [] \"\"; putStrLn out }`; claim untrusted_input -> logging.\n- default run: violated, details \"System.Process.Text.readProcess [haskell:Main.hs:6-8:main:function] -> Prelude.putStrLn\" -- a provenance: community row (process-extras overlay) for a Hackage package the program never imported.\n- --no-default-overlays: violated, details \"System.Process.readProcess ...\".\n- io-boundaries on the same file attributes System.Process.readProcess (the vouched row) -- the two arms disagree about one call.\nOn the mulul branch the same happens to System.Directory.getCurrentDirectory -> System.Directory.Extra.getCurrentDirectory (host_description source).\n\nThe VERDICT did not change in either repro; the attribution did. NOT CHECKED: whether the substitution changes any verdict anywhere (e.g. a base row carrying simultaneous / a different boundary than its overlay twin, the shape test_gate_prefers_vouched_rows was written for), and whether a community-reached disclosure is raised or lost.\n\nSUSPECTED mechanism, NOT verified: io_boundary.gate_named_entry orders hits vouched-first with getattr(h, \"unvouched\", False); TaintSource / TaintSink carry `community`, not `unvouched`, so every taint hit sorts as vouched and the overlay rows (merged IN FRONT of the base) win by declaration order. A second candidate: the hinted path, where _module_matches arm 2 may accept System.Process.Text for hint System.Process. Read both before fixing."  # 1d01
    fields:  # 1d01
      statement: "A taint source or sink matched for a call must be the same row io-boundaries attributes, and a vouched row must win over an unvouched community twin (ADR-0047, test_gate_prefers_vouched_rows). VIOLATED on dev e58250d: haskell readProcess -> putStrLn names System.Process.Text.readProcess (process-extras overlay) as the untrusted_input source; with --no-default-overlays it names System.Process.readProcess."  # 1d01
      root_cause: "NOT VERIFIED. Candidate: gate_named_entry sorts vouched-first on getattr(h, 'unvouched', False), and TaintSource/TaintSink carry 'community' instead, so all taint hits sort as vouched and the overlay rows merged in front of the base win. Second candidate: the hinted path via _module_matches arm 2."  # 1d01
- op: discuss  # 769e
  at: '2026-10-29T07:46:16Z'  # 769e
  by: agent  # 769e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 769e
  clock: 2  # 769e
  nonce: 769e  # 769e
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-10-29 (dev 4892851370). VERDICT: CURRENT; still violated. Filed repro re-run unchanged (Main.hs `import System.Process (readProcess)`; readProcess -> putStrLn; claim untrusted_input -> logging): default run names System.Process.Text.readProcess (source_module System.Process.Text, the process-extras community overlay); --no-default-overlays names System.Process.readProcess; `io-boundaries` on the same tree attributes System.Process.readProcess. Verdict `violated` in both arms, caveats [] in both. ROOT CAUSE, now traced (runtime wrap of named_lookup_arm, no repo edit): the module hint for this call is 'external', so the row choice goes to the GATE arm -- candidate 2 (hinted path / _module_matches arm 2) is RULED OUT here. In the gate (io_boundary.py:754, sort on getattr(h,'unvouched')): io-boundaries' IoPrimitive hits carry unvouched=[True,True,True,False,False] for Typed/Text/Text/base/base, so the vouched base row wins there; the taint hits carry NO unvouched attribute -- TaintSource has neither unvouched nor community (TaintSink and TaintSanitizer declare `community`, and the auto-derived sink rows from community overlays carry community=False) -- so every taint hit sorts as vouched and the overlay row merged in front wins by order. A probe that also sorted on `community` changed nothing, consistent with the flag never being set on these rows. So candidate 1 is right in mechanism and wrong in detail: the fix is to carry the io row's unvouched/community bit onto auto-derived TaintSource/TaintSink rows (or have the gate read one shared attribute), not only to rename the sort key. Still NOT CHECKED: a verdict change from a base/overlay pair whose boundaries differ (this pair's rows match: both ipc_recv + subprocess, simultaneous). Side observation, not this item: an explicit import list (`import System.Process (readProcess)`) yields no usable module hint for the bare call."  # 769e
