- op: discuss  # fd8f
  at: '2026-10-29T11:05:06Z'  # fd8f
  by: agent  # fd8f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # fd8f
  clock: 5  # fd8f
  nonce: fd8f  # fd8f
  message: "Fixed in PR #1940 (dev cf3e976b92). Auto-derived TaintSource/TaintSink rows now carry their io primitive's provenance as `community` (= IoPrimitive.unvouched), community taint-file sources are stamped like their sinks and sanitizers, and both row types expose `unvouched`, the attribute io_boundary.gate_named_entry sorts on -- so taint's row choice is the one io-boundaries makes. Filed repro re-run on merged dev cf3e976b92: the default run's untrusted_input source is now System.Process.readProcess (was System.Process.Text.readProcess), the same row --no-default-overlays and io-boundaries name; verdict `violated` unchanged. Tests: test_taint_prefers_vouched_rows.py through load_builtin_taint_catalog (reach; hint-less source and sink are the boot library; taint == io-boundaries for readProcess / readProcessWithExitCode; derived community rows and a community taint-file source are unvouched), mutation-checked per stamping site. Corpus A/B (verify-claims, generic claims; shellcheck, stack, git-bug, full-stack-fastapi-template): no verdict moved anywhere; stack's attribution moved from System.Process.Text / System.Directory.Extra / System.Process.Typed to System.Process / System.Directory, checked against the call sites' imports (release.hs, install-many-stack-releases.hs, Upgrade.hs import the boot libraries). check-self-claims: 18 unchanged. Root cause as traced in the 10-29 premise check: the gate arm (hint 'external'), not the hinted path. NOT a new item: a bare non-gated Haskell call keeps the hint 'external' even under an explicit import list -- deliberate since WI-lokun (only HASKELL_GATED_NAMES are stamped from the import context), so such calls are decided vouched-first; stack's src/Stack/Runners.hs (import RIO.Process, a typed-process wrapper) is one where the old Typed attribution was nearer, and both rows are subprocess. Still not checked: a base/overlay pair whose boundaries differ."  # fd8f
